# Platform conditionals outside crates/org-platform (ADR-0017 LNX-5).
#
# Each line is a source file and the number of platform predicates in it, as the check
# in crates/org-platform/tests/platform_conditionals.rs counts them: each `cfg` or
# `cfg_attr` attribute and each `cfg!` call that names target_os, target_vendor,
# target_env or target_family, and each other use of one of those four names. These
# are the files that had such predicates when the check was written (increment X1a).
#
# This list only shrinks. No count is raised and the total never rises (CI compares
# the list with the commit where the branch left v1-integration; a renamed or split
# file may appear under its new paths as long as the total does not rise): a new
# operating-system difference goes into crates/org-platform, behind a contract
# (docs/design/linux-host.md, section 1). When a file loses predicates, lower its
# count, or delete its line at zero, in the same change; the check fails until you do.
# The list is empty when Track X is complete (increment X6).
